review_comments.body:
Fixing the sibling-prefix false positive is right, but just deleting this and relying on `validateSubDir` leaves the dangerous case open. `validateSubDir` only rejects a sidecar *inside* the root. A sidecar that *contains* the root is accepted, and the sidecar storer creates and `RemoveAll`s `<sidecar>/<bucket>/...`.

Repro: `posix --sidecar /d /d/gwroot`, then `create-bucket gwroot` + `delete-bucket gwroot`. `SideCar.DeleteAttributes` runs `os.RemoveAll("/d/gwroot")` and wipes the whole gateway root, all buckets included. Creating `gwroot` also adds a phantom bucket `meta`, and `put-object gwroot/victim` writes sidecar files into bucket `victim`.

Please replace this with a two-way check (equal, or either one contains the other). Doing it in `validateSubDir` covers `--versioning-dir` too:

```go
if isDirBelowRoot(root, absDir) || isDirBelowRoot(absDir, root) {
	return "", fmt.Errorf("%v and the root directory %v must not be the same or nested in one another", dir, root)
}
```

The Helm chart already documents this intent: "Must not overlap /mnt/data or versioningDir".
